  "note": "Marked apron for GroundKind.STRIPED: weathered concrete hardstanding with worn traffic paint, generated as a reskin of art-source/templates/marked-apron-guide.png (prompt: marked-apron.prompt.txt). A 6x6 plate with dark gutters, no alpha; cut on the measured gutters, each cell trimmed 1 px inside its gutter. Frames 0-15 are apron.marked, 16-31 apron.keep-clear, each block's slot the exposed-edge mask (N=1 E=2 S=4 W=8); frames 32-35 are spare open apron and are not cut.\n\nBoth blocks use edge-faces-4x4: the renderer asks where the ground ends (a wall, or any neighbour drawn from another block), not where the walls are, so a run of apron is outlined by its painted line wherever it stops and the open field is plain concrete. apron.keep-clear fills the field with a diagonal hatch on a whole number of periods per cell, so a hatched zone tiles; it is the no-stand margin before a dock door and is placed as a surface override.\n\nThis replaces road.striped (urban-tileset-2), which the owner rejected: a dark blue-grey panel whose open cells repeated one edge piece."
